# Current events: what has been happening in town. Prices that moved, caravans in and out, bandits on the roads,
# crime, weddings and deaths, festivals, newcomers. Blanks come from the world (doc 30).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Prices

scene pr_herbs_up
when topic=prices topic.item=herbs topic.dir=up
a[healer] : Herbs at #topic.price# a bundle. How am I to treat anyone? | I can't afford my own remedies at #topic.price#.
a[cook] : #topic.price# for a bundle of herbs. My stew will taste of nothing.
a : Have you seen what herbs cost now? #topic.price#! | Herbs at #topic.price#. Robbery. | Who can afford herbs at #topic.price#?
b[merchant] : The store's near empty. I pay more, you pay more.
b[farmer] : Then gather your own. The hedges are full of them.
b[old] : In my day you picked them free by the road.
b : I saw. It's a scandal. | Everything's dearer this year. | I'll do without.
a?[friends] : I'll share what I have, if you're short.

scene pr_herbs_down
when topic=prices topic.item=herbs topic.dir=down
a : Herbs are cheap again, have you noticed? | Got a fat bundle of herbs for #topic.price#. | Herbs are going for #topic.price# now. Stock up.
b[merchant] : Cheap for you. Ruin for me.
b[healer] : Good. Maybe folk will come to me before they're dying.
b : About time. | I'll get some on the way home. | Good news, for once.
a : Buy while it lasts. | Exactly. | For once.

scene pr_meal_up
when topic=prices topic.item=meal topic.dir=up
a[child] : Why is supper so small? | Mama says bread costs too much now.
a : A hot meal costs #topic.price# now. #topic.price#! | Have you priced a meal lately? | I paid #topic.price# for a bowl of soup.
b[innkeeper] : Grain's dear, so food's dear. I don't set the price of grain.
b[farmer] : Don't look at me. I see none of that coin.
b[old] : I remember famine years. This isn't one. Yet.
b : Everything's going up. | We'll be eating grass soon. | Cook at home, then.
a : Not everything. My wages aren't. | Don't joke. | I do. Doesn't help.

scene pr_meal_down
when topic=prices topic.item=meal topic.dir=down
a : Food's cheaper this week. | A meal for #topic.price#. I nearly fell over. | The stores must be full.
b[innkeeper] : Cheaper for you. My margins are thin as broth.
b[farmer] : Good harvest. Somebody should thank us.
b : Thank the stars. | Eat while you can. | Long may it last.
a : Ha. | I intend to. | It won't.

scene pr_general_grumble
when topic=prices
weight 0.6
a : Prices, prices. That's all anyone talks about now. | My purse gets lighter every market. | Everything's #topic.price# this week, or near enough.
b[merchant] : Blame the roads. Every cart that's robbed is a price that rises.
b[official] : The council is aware of the matter.
b : Times are hard. | Mine too. | It'll settle.
a : The council's always aware. Never does anything. | They are. | It had better.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Caravans

scene cv_arrived
when topic=caravan topic.kind=arrived
a[merchant] : The caravan from #topic.where# is in. I'll have stock by tonight. | Finally, the #topic.where# wagons. My shelves were bare.
a[child] : Did you see the wagons? Big ones! With bells!
a : The caravan from #topic.where# came in today. | Wagons in from #topic.where#. | Did you see the carters from #topic.where#?
b[carter] : Rough road, but we made it. Barely.
b[innkeeper] : That'll mean a full house tonight.
b[guard] : I counted them in. Every crate.
b : About time. | Anything good on them? | Good. Maybe prices will fall.
a : Let's hope. | We'll see at market. | Maybe.

scene cv_left
when topic=caravan topic.kind=left
a : The wagons left for #topic.where# this morning. | Caravan's away to #topic.where#. | Saw the #topic.where# caravan go out the gate.
b[merchant] : My goods are on it. I'll not sleep till I hear.
b[carter] : I should be on it. Lame mule.
b[guard] : Light escort. I didn't like it.
b : Safe journey to them. | Long road to #topic.where#. | Let's hope it gets there.
a : Let's hope. | It is. | It will.

scene cv_raided
when topic=caravan topic.kind=raided
a[merchant] : The #topic.where# caravan was robbed. My whole order, gone. | Raided on the road from #topic.where#. I'm ruined.
a : Did you hear? The caravan from #topic.where# was raided. | Bandits hit the #topic.where# wagons. | They say the #topic.where# caravan never made it.
b[guard] : We need more blades on those roads, not fewer.
b[carter] : That could have been me. That should have been me.
b[old] : The roads were never safe. Never.
b : Were they hurt? | That's terrible. | That'll put prices up.
a : I don't know. | It is. | Everything will cost more now.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Bandits

scene bd_camp
when topic=bandits topic.kind=camp
a : There's a bandit camp out by #topic.where#, they say. | Travellers are being stopped near #topic.where#. | Don't take the road past #topic.where#.
b[guard] : We know. We're waiting on more spears before we go out.
b[carter] : I'll take the long way, then. Two days longer.
b[child] : I'd fight them!
b : Someone should clear them out. | I wasn't going to. | I'll stay home.
a : Someone should. | Good. | Wise.

scene bd_raided
when topic=bandits topic.kind=raided
a : The roads aren't safe any more. | Bandits again, on the way to #topic.where#. | Whole caravan stripped bare.
b[guard] : Every raid makes them bolder.
b[merchant] : And every raid makes me poorer.
b : What's the watch doing? | Shocking. | Bold, aren't they.
a : Not enough. | It is. | Too bold.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Crime

scene cr_theft
when topic=crime topic.kind=theft
a[guard] : We're looking into the matter of #topic.victim#'s loss. Seen anything? | A theft, under our noses.
a : Did you hear #topic.victim# was robbed? | Someone stole from #topic.victim#. | They say #topic.subject# robbed #topic.victim#.
b[merchant] : Lock your doors. I'm putting a second bolt on mine.
b[guard] : We'll find who did it.
b[old] : In my day thieves lost a paw.
b : That's awful. | Who'd do such a thing? | Poor #topic.victim#.
a : Keep your purse close. | Someone desperate. | Poor soul.

scene cr_assault
when topic=crime topic.kind=assault
a : #topic.victim# was attacked. In the street! | Someone beat #topic.victim# half senseless. | Did you hear about #topic.victim#?
b[healer] : I patched them up. They'll live, no thanks to whoever did it.
b[guard] : The watch is on it.
b : Terrible. | Is #topic.victim# all right? | What's the world coming to?
a : Barely. | Nobody knows. | Nothing good.

scene cr_arrest
when topic=crime topic.kind=arrest
a : The watch took #topic.subject# off to the gaol. | They arrested #topic.subject#! | #topic.subject#'s in the cells, I hear.
b[guard] : And there they'll stay.
b[old] : Always knew that one was trouble.
b : What did they do? | About time. | I'd never have thought it.
a : Nobody's saying. | I suppose. | Nor would I.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Life in town

scene lf_marriage
when topic=life topic.kind=marriage
a[old] : #topic.subject# and #topic.where# are wed, did you hear? I remember them as pups.
a : #topic.subject# married #topic.where#! | Did you hear? #topic.subject# and #topic.where# are wed. | There was a wedding. #topic.subject# and #topic.where#.
b[child] : Was there cake?
b[female] : About time. Everyone could see it. | They'll make a fine pair.
b : Good for them. | I never thought they'd do it. | They'll be happy, I think.
a : They will. | Nor did I. | Let's hope.

scene lf_death
when topic=life topic.kind=death
a[old] : #topic.subject# has passed. That's another of my generation gone. | They buried #topic.subject# this morning.
a : Did you hear #topic.subject# died? | #topic.subject# is gone. | #topic.where# is grieving; #topic.subject# died.
b[priest] : I said the words over them. It was a gentle end.
b[child] : Is #topic.subject# with the stars now?
b : I'm sorry to hear it. | May they rest. | #topic.where# must be heartbroken.
a : So am I. | Rest well. | They are.

scene lf_apprentice
when topic=life topic.kind=apprentice
a : #topic.subject#'s apprenticed to #topic.where# now. | #topic.where# took on #topic.subject# as an apprentice. | Young #topic.subject# is learning a trade at last.
b[old] : Good. Idle paws find mischief.
b[apprentice] : Poor thing. The first year is the worst.
b : That's good news. | Good for them. | About time.
a : It is. | It is. | Ha.

scene lf_succession
when topic=life topic.kind=succession
a : #topic.subject# has taken over the old work. | So #topic.subject# has the shop now. | #topic.subject# stepped into the dead one's place.
b[old] : Life goes on. Somebody has to do the work.
b : Will they be any good? | They'll do well. | Big boots to fill.
a : We'll see. | I hope so. | Very big.

scene lf_newcomer
when topic=newcomer
a : Have you met #topic.subject#? Just arrived. | There's a new face in town. #topic.subject#, they're called. | #topic.subject#'s moved in down the street.
b[old] : New blood. Good. We need it.
b[child] : Do they have pups? Can I play with them?
b[guard] : I'll keep an eye on them.
b : Not yet. What are they like? | Where are they from? | Welcome to them.
a : Quiet, so far. | Somewhere far. | Indeed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Festivals

scene fs_today
when topic=festival topic.when=today
a[child] : It's #here.festival#! It's #here.festival#! | Will there be music? Will there be sweets?
a : Joy of #here.festival# to you! | Are you going to the celebration? | #here.festival# at last.
b[old] : Every year it comes round faster.
b[innkeeper] : Busiest day of my year. Pray for me.
b[guard] : Celebrate all you like. Just don't fight.
b : And to you! | Wouldn't miss it. | It's been a long wait.
a : Come and find me later. | See you there. | Too long.

scene fs_soon
when topic=festival topic.when=soon
a : #here.festival# is soon. Are you ready? | Only a few days to #here.festival#. | What will you wear for #here.festival#?
b[child] : I can't wait! I can't!
b[merchant] : I've ordered extra of everything.
b : Nearly ready. | I've not even thought about it. | My old best, as always.
a : Good. | Better start thinking. | Ha.
